# Line ending normalization.
#
# This is a Linux-only project: enforce LF in the repository and in the
# working tree so that Windows checkouts don't end up with CRLF.
#
# `text=auto` lets git auto-detect text vs. binary and normalizes CRLF -> LF
# on commit. `eol=lf` keeps the working tree on LF even on Windows.
# Together this makes line-ending differences across systems a non-issue.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Explicitly mark common binary types so they are never normalized.
*.png  binary
*.jpg  binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif  binary
*.ico  binary
*.webp binary
*.bmp  binary
*.so   binary
*.a    binary
*.o    binary
*.dll  binary
*.exe  binary
*.zip  binary
*.gz   binary
*.tar  binary
*.7z   binary
*.db   binary
*.sqlite binary
*.pdf  binary
